// ACCEPTANCE FIXED 2026-08-05 (Eric's ruling: compile-reject):
// extract_cast_type's contains_bottom now descends composite
// constructors, so both modes reject deterministically (pinned in
// findings/cast-bottom-composite-aug2026/). STILL OPEN here: the
// SEED (async module-load order varies per process, shifting all
// id/tvar minting) and the settle ORDER-SENSITIVITY (Array<⊥> vs
// open depending on unification order) — latent typechecker
// determinism work.
// ORIGINAL ANALYSIS (2026-08-05, aug04d2 fuzz/000000): NONDETERMINISTIC COMPILE
// ACCEPTANCE — ~20% of fresh processes CompileErr ("str::parse
// requires a concrete return type"), ~80% compile and run (parse
// errors at runtime, ?-propagates, empty trace). Either MODE can be
// the failing one; 40-50-run hammers reproduce on abd4339a AND
// 0a0014eb (pre-existing, NOT A1). Two stacked causes established
// with GXDBG_PARSE + GXDBG_RESOLVE:
// (1) SEED: per-process stdlib module compile ORDER varies (async
//     ModuleResolver load completion order) — B2L-INS traces show
//     the bytes module's members registering in different sequence,
//     shifting every downstream BindId/TVar mint (ids differ 1752 vs
//     1764 across runs). Harmless alone; detcheck's counter
//     normalization is blind to it by design.
// (2) AMPLIFIER (the real defect): the parse call site's return
//     settle is ORDER-SENSITIVE — cast_typ resolves Some(Array(⊥))
//     under one unification order and stays None under another; the
//     None lands on resolve_static's LOUD tc1 path → CompileErr,
//     while runs that leave the site to the lazy bind swallow the
//     same failure (SWALLOWED-LAZY-TC1) and proceed. Note
//     Array(Bottom) as an ACCEPTED cast target is itself suspect
//     (the jul14b extract_cast_type ⊥-member family, shaped as
//     Array-of-⊥ which that fix's net misses).
// Deterministic-correct outcome TBD (Eric): likely compile-reject
// (unconstrained parse return), which would also want the settle
// made order-independent and/or module load order made
// deterministic. No wrong VALUES ever produced — acceptance only.
array::window(#n: i64:1, str::parse("notanumber")?, never())
